## Context

Follow-up of 1395 (PR #2090). The author asked why delegation orange is
sometimes a long bar in an agent's main row and sometimes a short tick on its
own row. Answer: long = a blocking delegation (e.g. a forked /gaze Skill call,
2–4.5 min in d77349fe, the agent waits); short = a launch that returns at
once (background Agent call, ~0.7 min), pushed to a lower row by overlapping
calls, its work shown in the child's own lane. The author asked for both
display aids, 2026-10-31, with a guard against "spaghettifying" the graph.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each delegation call is marked `blocking` or `launch`, by a documented
      rule with unit tests (e.g. the tool input's background flag where the
      runtime records one, else whether the call ends before its child agent's
      span ends); unknown falls back to plain delegation
- [ ] Blocking delegations are drawn distinctly (hatched or darker orange) and
      the legend says what it means; the tooltip names the mode
- [ ] Thin connectors run from each launch tick to the start of the child
      agent's span in its lane (child matched to its launching call by a
      recorded link, not by time proximity alone; unmatched launches draw no
      connector)
- [ ] A visible checkbox disables/enables the connectors (default on), no
      reload needed
- [ ] Launches that start at the same time (or within a few pixels at the
      current zoom) get vertical paths offset so no two overlap; recomputed on
      zoom
- [ ] Self-contained page; any JSON change is additive only (test); existing
      tests pass
- [ ] Rendered for d77349fe-10eb-46dd-a58c-d5723e771c4d, headless Firefox
      screenshot with connectors on and off; the author checks interaction
